./iterations/iter_008/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:5:The critique is that several claims are not yet theorem-ready. The main gaps are not conceptual contradictions, but missing measurability, policy-reduction, and value-comparison details. The strongest claim that survives is a fixed finite-\(T\), finite-grid no-gap theorem under common domination of payoff-weighted reward measures, provided policies are formalized as public-prefix randomized kernels up to the dominating measures.
