./iterations/iter_008/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:37:   If both \(L_\theta(q)\) uniformly over all \(q\) and \(V_\theta^G\) are within \(\varepsilon\), then regret values shift by at most about \(2\varepsilon\), and the full-vs-finite no-gap error is about \(4\varepsilon\). The report’s \(O(\varepsilon)\) is fine informally, but a theorem needs constants. Also, uniform approximation over all Borel policies is essentially a total-variation-type requirement, so this may not cover many nondominated examples.
