./iterations/iter_007/idea_01/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:44:- **Non-Borel label stress test:** with \(T=2\), \(G=\{1/3,2/3\}\), \(P_1=x\), and \(P_2=1\) on \(A\), \(P_2=1/2\) off \(A\), finite subclasses have value \(0\). For Borel policies, full value is \(1/6\) if \(A\) is non-Borel: regret \(<1/6\) would require a Borel separator for \(A\).
./iterations/iter_007/idea_01/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:46:- **Borel version sanity check:** if \(A\) is Borel in the same construction, full value is \(0\). So nondomination alone is not the obstruction; the obstruction is measurability/closedness.
