./iterations/iter_002/idea_01/explorer_01.md:3:The law-aware oracle lemma is valid in the finite-horizon, known-law, exogenous/action-independent model, with `sup_a` rather than `max_a`. For every known exogenous law on \(P_{1:T}\), a horizon-aware learner can achieve regret at most \(T/K\) by maximizing conditional expected reward over a \(K\)-grid at each time. Taking \(K=T\) gives \(O(1)\) regret, so no nontrivial fixed-law tail condition can be necessary under these quantifiers.
