./iterations/iter_002/idea_01/explorer_01.md:60:**Measurability is fine.** Since \([0,1]^T\) is standard Borel, regular conditional probabilities exist. For finite \(\mathcal G_K\), choosing the smallest grid maximizer is measurable up to null-history choices.
